   "prompt": "Fourth Opus review of auto-approve: FAIL (3 high). Root problem: the guard checks a hardened git environment but the session then runs plain git in its own environment and config, so checks and execution diverge (hardened command only logged, system gitconfig unchecked, wrong environment checked, config helpers and PATH trust). Fix it by construction with a redesign: auto-approve no longer covers plain git. Add a subcommand 'swarm handbuild git SUBCOMMAND [args]' (in tools/auto-approve-policy.mjs plus the CLI dispatch where 'swarm handbuild' is handled in tools/swarm.mjs or tools/handbuild.mjs) that is the ONLY thing a policy window can approve for git: it (a) finds git itself at a pinned absolute path (/usr/bin/git, /opt/homebrew/bin/git or /usr/local/bin/git, first that exists, resolved by realpath, owned by root or the current user and not group or world writable, never from PATH), (b) runs it with a fully clean environment it builds itself (PATH=/usr/bin:/bin, HOME set to an empty temp dir, GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL and GIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM at /dev/null, GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1, GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0, no other GIT variables and none inherited) plus -c core.fsmonitor=false -c core.hooksPath=/dev/null -c credential.helper= -c core.sshCommand=ssh -c protocol.ext.allow=never, (c) does every policy check (branch and HEAD binding, clean tree for switch, trusted origin URL from owner config checked against remote get-url --push --all, push mapping, repo-local config allow-list, hooks in the common git dir, rate limits, kill switch, covered literal paths for add, commit with -m only) and the command in the SAME process with the same clean environment, atomically, and (d) logs every call. The guard then approves only commands whose first words are exactly the installed swarm handbuild git form (reuse the strict swarm invocation matcher of orchestrator mode: installed swarm path only) and treats every plain git (any path to git, relative or absolute: keep the name-based classification of the main guard so absolute-path git is still classified as git and owner-only commands stay owner-only, only the policy-trusted match is strict) as not covered by any policy window. Remaining findings to fix with a test each in tests/auto-approve.test.mjs: git add accepts only the double-dash option, no backslash normalisation, no --pathspec-from-file, -f or --chmod; symlinked folders for new files: stop at the first existing path part and reject it when it is a symlink or resolves elsewhere; folder entries rejected and every real write path re-checked at edit time against allowed folders and the code-extension rule (add .html .svg .mdx .mts .ps1 to code extensions); remote settings allowed only from repo-local config; the policy file override via SWARM_CONFIG and SWARM_POLICY_FILE ignored everywhere including the standing merge path unless the signed test marker exists; the missing-stats bug: the policy must initialise stats.json itself with an initialised marker on first use so policy approvals can switch on, and a missing file after initialisation stays unreadable (limit reached); SAFE_SWARM anchored so no other verb can sit before a safe one and 'swarm handbuild list' stays allowed; the push-mapping and inner hooksPath checks fail closed on git errors; a missing policy row in the guard denies instead of throwing; drop git show from the allowed list or document it; protect the ssh config and known_hosts files under the home directory from session writes. Update docs/auto-approve.md for the swarm handbuild git form. Keep every guard, approval and swarm-merge test passing.",
